Copyright: 2025-2026 Çağan ERGÜN <73942784+caganerg@users.noreply.github.com>
           2006-2008 Aurélien Croc (AP²C) <aurelien@ap2c.org>
License: GPL-2
 These files carry material transcribed from OpenPrinting SpliX
 (https://github.com/OpenPrinting/splix), which is GPL-2.0-only. They are
 therefore a derived work and this package cannot be relicensed as GPL-2+.
 .
 The list changed shape in the 2.0 line without changing what is derived: the
 engine moved out of the binary into the spl2-core crate. What this paragraph
 used to call src/spl.rs is now crates/spl2-core/src/qpdl.rs, and the geometry
 rules that used to sit in src/main.rs are now split between
 crates/spl2-core/src/geometry.rs and crates/spl2-core/src/engine.rs. The
 files moved; the transcription did not grow.
 .
 crates/spl2-core/src/qpdl.rs states the derivation in its own header: the
 QPDL wire constants, the PJL job header and its exact line order, the 17-byte
 page header layout and the Algo 0x11 RLE band encoding all come from SpliX's
 qpdl.cpp, compress.cpp, algo0x11.cpp and printer.cpp.
 .
 crates/spl2-core/src/geometry.rs and crates/spl2-core/src/engine.rs
 transcribe SpliX's geometry rules, each cited at the function that implements
 it: the page-width computation from document.cpp, the hard margin and
 column-major band fill from compress.cpp _compressBandedPage, the duplex
 mapping from request.cpp, and the "halve the band height at 300x300" rule
 from compress.cpp.
 .
 crates/spl2-core/src/media.rs holds one derived constant: the 12.5 pt hard
 margin, which follows SpliX's ML-2165 override.
 .
 src/main.rs is the frozen 1.x CUPS filter front end. It now delegates the
 protocol and the geometry to spl2-core and keeps the SpliX citations at the
 call sites that explain the byte-for-byte behaviour. It is not installed by
 this package; it is kept in the source tree until the migration's P11 gate
 passes.
 .
 ppd/samsung-ml2160.ppd takes its QPDL paper-source codes, media-type
 keywords and band size from the sibling PPDs upstream SpliX ships for this
 engine family (ml1910, ml2010, ml2525, ml1640, ml2510), as its own comments
 record. It is likewise not installed by this package and is kept as project
 data.
 .
 crates/spl2-core/src/raster.rs and src/golden.rs are NOT derived from SpliX:
 raster.rs implements the CUPS Raster container format, and golden.rs is this
 project's own test harness. Each mentions SpliX once, as a cross-reference
 rather than as transcribed material.
Comment: The upstream notice was transcribed from the SpliX 2.0.1 source
 (Debian source package splix 2.0.1-1, from http://splix.ap2c.org/). Every
 file this project draws from — qpdl.cpp, compress.cpp, algo0x11.cpp,
 document.cpp, printer.cpp and request.cpp — carries the same header line,
 "(C) 2006-2008, Aurélien Croc (AP²C)", and the package's own debian/copyright
 names Aurélien Croc <aurelien@ap2c.org> as the upstream author under GPL
 version 2 only. The PPD values come from ppd/samsung.drv.in and the defs it
 imports, headed "(C) 2007, Aurélien Croc (AP²C)", which the range above
 covers.

Files: crates/pappl-sys/*
